    25	The bars above only count when measured under these definitions. A run that departs from them cannot close an NS obligation.
    26	
    27	**P1 pinned reads that never block writers.**
    28	1. Readers and writers share one hot set: at least 50% of reads target subjects written in the previous 60 s (section 2.1 active set).
    29	2. 10% of subgraph reads are issued as two or more queries at the same named basis, and the driver commits a mutation to those same
    30	   subjects between the steps. The answer must equal the oracle's answer at the requested basis, never the latest state.
    31	3. Every P1 window contains at least one maintenance event (XTDB compaction; QLever index rebuild or delta merge; index-layer catch-up).
