   165	   B is served by index I only if w(I) ≥ B.position; otherwise it waits up to 250 ms (the P3 lag bar) and then routes to a fallback that
   166	   has the position (the source of truth's own query surface, or another index), and the receipt records the route. No index ever
   167	   answers for a basis it has not reached.
