    10	   constraints; expressions and errors; plans, costing and recursion; negation at coherent cuts; aggregates;
    11	   cancellation and resources; atomic writes, receipts and recovery; reuse and maintained supports; bitemporal history,
    12	   presence, deletion and cascades; public TypeScript integration.
