    67	### 0.1.0-draft
    68	
    69	First draft (88 obligations). Superseded.
    70	
    71	## 1. How to read this contract
    72	
    73	- **One obligation is one binary fact.** It has an id, a statement, lanes, case selections, oracles, entrypoints, profiles, a closure (rules, modes, thresholds), mutation controls, the PLAN contracts it traces, sources, a grounding label and a verifier mode.
    74	- **Every status is OPEN.** No acceptance receipt exists for any obligation.
    75	- **Authority for goals and targets.** `lab/SCOPE.md`, `lab/NORTH-STAR.md`, `lab/TARGETS.md` and `lab/research/SAM-pasted-numbers-2026-11-07.md` (Sam, 2026-11-07), compiled with `RULINGS.md` into `obligations.json`. Correctness is the floor on every priority: a fast wrong answer scores zero.
    76	- **Values this contract chose.** Thresholds whose source says `derived`, the reader read mix and window lengths in `load-contract.json`, and the A0 allowances in `budgets.json` are values no source states; they are fixed so evaluation is mechanical, and changing one is a contract version.
    77	- **Artifacts.** `obligations.json` (authority), `load-contract.json`, `budgets.json`, `capability-matrix.md`, this file. All generated.
    78	
    79	## 2. Done predicate (PLAN v1.1 section 1)
    80	
    81	```
    82	done(T) = for one identified integrated profile T per surface
    83	          AND over lanes { xtdb-xtql, xtdb-sql, qlever-sparql }
    84	          AND over sections { G1..G10, R, S, L }
    85	            closed(section, lane, T)
    86	          with every receipt FRESH on T (no carry-forward into final acceptance)
    87	
    88	 retained evidence --> VC / VA / VM / VV validity --> closure rules recompute verdicts --> obligation
    89	   (runs/objects)       (acyclic: VC <- VA <- VM, VV)    from retained bytes             --> section --> lane --> done
    90	```
    91	
    92	
    93	Status algorithm:
    94	
    95	```
    96	for each lane L and integrated profile T:
    97	  for each obligation O with L in O.lanes:
    98	    key = L if O.receiptScope == 'lane' else (O.layer, T.composition[O.layer].engine, imageDigest, configSha256, slot)  # RULINGS Q28
    99	    A = acceptance receipts for (O.id, key) on T that pass VA (using VC records they cite)
   100	    closed(O, L, T) = O.grounding != 'policy-pending' and every case set of O is pinned
   101	                      and A non-empty and every rule in O.closure.rules holds by its recompute
   102	                      and VV-valid verifier coverage exists per VERIFIER_MODES[verifierMode(O)]
   103	  closed(section, L, T) = all closed(O, L, T) for O with section in O.goals
   104	done(T) = closed for every section and lane, with every receipt fresh on T (APPLICABILITY.finalAcceptance)
   105	```
   106	
   107	**Lane accounting.** Every read substep records exactly one language: xtql (native.select), sql (selectSql), sparql (QLever native). A lane receipt counts a task only when every relational substep is in the lane's language. A task with a relational substep in another language, or with a host step not listed below, counts for neither XTDB language.
