910:- Expected answers come from the independent oracles, never from a system under test: O-REPLAY for database state and values, O-DOMAIN for domain outputs and effects under WORLD_W0, or a frozen hand derivation with a citation (O-HAND).
915:- Each GS obligation binds only its own scenario: it selects its own tag and named cases, names exactly its own bars plus T-RUNS, and its receipt carries an ns-run whose measurement is its own scenario id (RULINGS Q26).
918:- All 20 run on every composition being compared, and the final acceptance reruns all 20 fresh.
923:Role: measurement size for P1 to P5 and the golden scenarios; not a target in itself (lab/SCOPE.md section 2 item 2). Source: lab/TARGETS.md section 2 (year-one scale; rungs 10k, 100k, 1m, 10m) and section 1 P4 (history depths 1, 3, 10); qualification/benchmark-contract.json (topologies, query families); acceptance review r1 finding 13. Rungs: 10000, 100000, 1000000, 10000000; every count and stratum scales proportionally with the rung; hub in-degree is 1% of the rung's entities; shares are identical at every rung. At year one: {"entities": 10000000, "activeDomainFacts": 100000000, "retainedFactsMin": 150000000, "retainedFactsNote": "TARGETS section 2: retained history 150M to 500M facts per year; the history strata below give about 162M retained facts"}. Facts per entity: 10 active domain facts: label (string), risk score (number, approximate), pay rate (decimal, scale 2), hours (integer), headcount (integer), flag (boolean), group (ref), category (string, skewed), start date (datetime), status changed at (datetime). Written through public writes (EP-WRITER, or EP-BULK for the initial load), every command ACKed with a receipt, no unresolved outcome.
952:Counted separately: entities per tenant, domain facts, structural facts, assertion versions and retirements, config facts, journal, claim, receipt and feed metadata, maintenance relations, engine rows or triples by physical role, edges, presence events, corrections.
1007:### 8.7 Composition identity (TARGETS 4.1, RULINGS Q28)
1017:| layerSwaps | layers are swapped one at a time under matched workloads at small rungs (current-index candidates on P1 and P4; history candidates on past-basis reads and GS.12; source candidates on P2 and P3); only the two or three best compositions go on to end-to-end validation with the golden scenarios |
1018:| scopeKey | an engine-scope receipt's key is (layer, the engine assigned to that layer, its image digest, configuration hash and slot), derived from the composition, never from engineOfLane |
1020:### 8.8 Erasure (TARGETS section 7, RULINGS Q24)
1024:| status | PROVISIONAL product ruling (RULINGS Q24), flagged for Sam: explain at a pre-erasure basis shows the marker, not the value |
1025:| boundary | the boundary is the erasure commit's publication; a read that started before it may return the old value; every read that starts after it, at any basis including bases before the erasure, returns ErasedValue {erasedAt} in place of the value |
1027:| reproduction | reproduction contracts (cursor stability, bit-for-bit explain, GS.12) hold modulo erasure: answers are compared with erased values replaced by their markers |
1029:| restore | the erasure ledger is kept apart from the data and replayed after any restore or rebuild |
1034:### 8.9 Evaluator counterexamples (RULINGS Q26)
1036:Every obligation declares at least one mode. 'single-execution' runs each selected case once, so executions equal selections; NS and GS obligations use it explicitly (RULINGS Q26). Other modes (current, reopen, engine-restart) each run every selected case once more. A secondary threshold (RULINGS Q25) is measured and reported against its value every run; missing it never fails or blocks an obligation, and it never feeds a closure rule other than CR-METRICS.
1040:| CX-CALIBRATION-EMPTY | CR-CALIBRATION | a VC record with an empty values list | an empty requirement set fails closed |
1041:| CX-CALIBRATION-MISSING | CR-CALIBRATION, CR-NS | a VC record that omits one threshold an NS obligation names | every named threshold needs a record |
1172:- Statement: Every lane accepts every integer in [-(2^53-1), 2^53-1]; on every qualified write route (the Triplex writer, the bulk import lane, replay and restore: RANGE-OUT-WRITER, RANGE-OUT-BULK, RANGE-OUT-REPLAY, RANGE-OUT-RESTORE) every CS-RANGE-OUT case (integers beyond the lane's declared LANE_INTEGER_RANGE, for QLever beyond +/-2^59) fails atomically with E-VALUE-OUT-OF-RANGE before any mutation, with no residue on any access path, and is never wrapped, widened or rounded. Bare native wire access is a diagnostic surface, not a qualified route: QLever's native wrap there is matrix row 51 (KNOWN-LIMIT KL-Q1) and diagnostic D-Q-INT60, never a failure of this obligation (RULINGS Q23).
1182:- Statement: Every CS-DECIMAL case, per DECIMAL_RULES (RULINGS Q18) and the operation, conversion and scale tables DECIMAL_OPS, DECIMAL_CONVERSIONS and DECIMAL_SCALE_EVOLUTION (RULINGS Q22), one named case per row, plus DECIMAL_TESTS (adjacent large decimals, negatives, zero, scale boundaries, arithmetic intermediates, every query and serialization path, an independent order-key check, and input capture before normalization): each decimal attribute declares precision and scale; precision <= 15 is stored as a scaled integer (DEC-P15-SCALED), larger precision as an order-preserving decimal string (DEC-P16-STRING); both round-trip exactly on every surface; every comparison with integer or number, equality included, is preflight E-MIXED-FAMILY (DEC-CROSS-FAMILY-PREFLIGHT) and exact after explicit conversion (DEC-CONVERTED-COMPARE); results beyond the precision fail with E-DECIMAL-OVERFLOW, bare / with E-DECIMAL-BARE-DIVIDE, decimal to integer with a fraction with E-DECIMAL-FRACTION, and a narrowing migration that would lose digits with E-DECIMAL-NARROWING, atomically; range rules (for example 'pay rate at or above 16.50') compare in exact numeric order on the repository, fragments and documented raw channel; a value with more fractional digits than the scale (DEC-SCALE-EXCESS) or outside the precision (DEC-PRECISION-EXCESS) fails with E-DECIMAL-UNREPRESENTABLE, never rounded; kernel arithmetic over decimals is exact.
1188:- Sources: RULINGS Q18; RULINGS Q22; lab/TARGETS.md section 3 (decimal value kind on the critical path for goal 1); lab/research/SAM-pasted-numbers-2026-11-07.md section 3.
1349:- Statement: At P-YEAR-ONE the point, getMany, selective-filter and reverse-ref classes resolve through a key-bounded access path (OBS-PLAN-ACCESS) with O-REPLAY answers; their p50 ratio between P-RUNG-1M and P-YEAR-ONE is reported against T-LAT-RATIO-10M-1M as a secondary measurement with no authority to block done (RULINGS Q25).
1378:- Statement: Recursive reads over every benchmark-contract topology (chain, tree, diamond, cycle, high-fanout, skewed-hotset) return O-REPLAY answers in the lane language at P-RUNG-1M and P-YEAR-ONE and stay bounded (round and row bounds, budgets, cancellation and typed resource errors per G3.recursion.read-only-frontier and goal 6); their p99 is reported against T-RECURSION-P99-MS as a secondary measurement with no authority to block done (RULINGS Q25).
1411:- Statement: The correlated NOT EXISTS controls written in raw SQL and raw XTQL over the documented raw dataset return only `two` (the QLever raw cell is exception RX-Q29, qualified by R.raw.mapped-recipes).
1430:- Statement: Every C5-* case of CS-CONFLICT: Equal-valued duplicates are not conflicts (one value, several supports); a conflict is two or more distinct live values of a cardinality-one attribute at the basis; get and getMany fail with E-CONFLICTING-VALUES listing every conflicted entity and attribute (compared on _tag, reason and the set of {entityId, attribute}, AMB-13); counts, ordering, includes and negation fail with it when a referenced attribute is conflicted for any candidate; find also fails with it when a returned document contains a conflicted attribute even if the filter avoids it, while a projection that omits the attribute succeeds (RS-FIND-CONFLICT, RULINGS Q21 AMB-17, provisional, flagged for Sam); reads that neither reference nor return a conflicted attribute are unaffected; the values(attribute) relation lists every live value with its supports; the raw convenience shape returns its documented indicator and never certifies equivalence.
1454:- Statement: Every CS-SUPPORT case returns the AG-SUM-I, AG-SUM-F, AG-COUNT and AG-SUM-ONE-ENTITY answers on the repository and supported native fragments: SUM runs over the bag of distinct solution rows, so equal values on distinct entities each count, while two equal-valued assertions on one entity are one value with two supports and one binding row (SUM 10, COUNT 1; RULINGS Q21 AMB-09, provisional, flagged for Sam); integer results project as IntegerValue text (AG-INT-RESULT).
1592:- Statement: Every C6-* case: direct match and Datalog queries over :_tx/change and :_tx/changed-entity, transactions(), transactionsForEntity and transactionByCommand return O-REPLAY's outputs per JOURNAL_RULES: creation order (JN-ORDER), staged facts visible to later operations of the same command (JN-STAGED), bit-exact -0.0 change values (JN-NEGZERO, RULINGS Q21 AMB-04, provisional, flagged for Sam) and the documented and testkit-pinned fields (JN-FIELDS); whole-journal byte identity of a physically slimmed journal is checked against a separate T0-capture baseline (C6-SLIM-BYTE-IDENTICAL).
