   662	### 6.1 O-REPLAY (independent Python event replay)
   663	
   664	- **Inputs.** The captured command intent (ordered submissions with operations, typed values in canonical encoding, entity ids and types, valid intervals, preconditions, meta, enforcement mode and rules, nested-transaction structure), schema releases, and durable-decision evidence (engine commit evidence or the log of record read back, and the fault witness). ACK receipts bind only generated identities: assertion ids, txIds and recorded instants.
   665	- **Clocks.** Recorded instants are not assumed monotonic in position order; separate runtimes supply their own clocks (PLAN C1). Histories with equal and with decreasing recorded instants are first-class cases (EV-SAME-R, EV-DECREASING-R, CS-TEMPORAL decreasing-clock).
   666	- **R independent of P.** A cut is (scope, P, optional R, V). Recorded visibility is `recordedPosition <= P` and, when R is bound, `recordedAt <= R`, evaluated independently: an assertion with a later position but an earlier instant is invisible at P below its position, and an assertion at a lower position with an instant above R is invisible at R.
   667	- **Position accounting.** Positions are derived by the oracle from the committed order: one position per Triplex transact, nested transacts inside one outer transaction take consecutive positions in callback order and share one engine commit; the oracle checks every receipt position against its own and fails the run on a mismatch.
   668	- **Outcomes.** The oracle derives each command's expected outcome from intent, order, preconditions, enforcement (CN-NEW-OR-WORSENED) and durable-decision evidence (COMMIT_OUTCOMES), then compares the receipts' outcomes afterwards. A receipt never decides which command is valid or committed.
   669	- **Outputs.** Complete assertion metadata; raw-lifetime and as-of snapshot history; entity models (card-one value or E-CONFLICTING-VALUES per C5; card-many per CARD_MANY_ORDER; absent optional as a missing property; includes at the same basis; timelines); transaction records with ordered changes and the logical journal facts (C6); cursor page sequences; support counts; C1 eligibility routes (for O-PLAN); arithmetic, comparison and aggregate results per section 4; analytic scale counts per population stratum (SCALE_POPULATION, section S).
   670	- **Independence.** Python stdlib only; imports no repository code; its own exact integers and decimals, IEEE binary64 (via struct) and codepoint ordering; no casefolding.
   671	- **Self-checks before ACCEPTED.** Reproduce O-HAM finite-nine, O-CFG8 tiny-v4 and the O-EVT cut semantics where domains overlap; unit tests for every table row of section 4.
   672	
   683	### 6.3 O-OBS protocols
   684	
   685	| Protocol | Evidence fields | Verdict |
   686	| --- | --- | --- |
   687	| OBS-CANCEL | requestId, connectionId, tCancelRequested, tCallerSettled, callerError, transportAck {kind, t}, engineActiveSamples [{t, activeQueryIds}], tDrained, reuseQueryId, tReuseOk | PASS iff callerError matches E-CANCELLED or E-TIMEOUT as the case pins, transportAck observed, the request id absent from every engine sample after tDrained with tDrained - tCancelRequested <= T-DRAIN-MS, sample gaps <= 1000 ms over [tCancelRequested, tDrained + 5000 ms], and the reuse query on the same connection succeeds |
   688	| OBS-PREABORT | requestId, engineStatementLog [{t, tag}], coverage | PASS iff zero engine statements carry the request id over the full coverage window |
   689	| OBS-CONNECTIONS | poolDeclarations [{label, max}], engineConnectionSamples [{t, label, count}], baseline, tClose | PASS iff every sample <= declared max and the count equals baseline within T-CONN-RELEASE-MS after tClose |
   690	| OBS-SCRATCH | relation, countBefore, countAfter, resolutionReceipts | PASS iff countAfter = countBefore for every scratch relation and every unknown working outcome is resolved |
   691	| OBS-NO-MUTATION | engineMutationCounterBefore, engineMutationCounterAfter, counterSource | PASS iff the engine's committed-transaction or update counter is unchanged across the read |
   692	| OBS-RESOURCE | forecast {memory, disk}, peaks [{owner, rss, disk, t}], envelope | PASS iff every peak <= forecast <= envelope (and <= T-PLANNER-MEM-BYTES where named) |
   693	| OBS-AVAILABILITY | tFailure, probes [{t, kind: write\|read, outcome}] | PASS iff a write and a read both succeed at some t <= tFailure + T-AVAIL-WINDOW-MS with no manual restart event |
   694	| OBS-SCALE-COUNT | population, countQueryCaseResult, analyticCount | PASS iff the count query's answer equals O-REPLAY's analytic count |
   695	| OBS-WORK | operation, engineWorkUnits {rowsScanned, rowsWritten, triplesTouched, bytesWritten}, source | ratio of work units between the compared operations, evaluated against the named witness threshold |
   696	| OBS-MAINTENANCE | kind, tStart, tEnd, lagSamples | events present; lag statistics against the named threshold |
   697	| OBS-ERASURE-SCAN | inventoryEntry, location, scanMethod, plaintextHits, derivedChannelHits, keyDestroyedEvidence, tScan | PASS iff every PROTECTED_COPY_INVENTORY location of the lane is scanned after the erasure published and shows zero plaintext and zero derived-channel hits, or carries evidence that the per-subject key was destroyed |
   698	| OBS-WATERMARK | readId, basisPosition, servingIndex, watermarkAtRead, waitMs, route, fallbackIndex | PASS iff no read was answered by an index whose watermark was below the basis position, every wait before routing is within T-WATERMARK-WAIT-MS, and every route is recorded |
   699	| OBS-ACK-ORDER | commitPosition, tCurrentIndexReached, tAck, ackSender | PASS iff the source of truth sent every ACK and tAck >= tCurrentIndexReached for every commit |
   700	| OBS-FAULT-TRANSITIONS | transition, t, durableEvidenceObject | the last witnessed transition is the last one whose durable evidence is present after the crash |
