   992	### 8.6 Budgets
   993	
   994	Budgets are re-frozen after EXP-N02 measures the A0 controls, in a create-only budget-freeze receipt (A0 control measurements at every rung, this file's sha256), before any candidate is evaluated against them. No candidate comparison may cite a budget that has not been re-frozen. A hypothesis's predicted cost never sets its own allowance. Changing a budget creates a new profile version; loosening an NS bar needs Sam. A0 = the ledger-only baseline profile (status-quo adapters, no projection), measured on the same slot configuration, writer trace and rung. Where A0 cannot complete a rung, only the absolute bars and caps apply there and the failure is recorded. Every promotion and the final acceptance compare the integrated candidate with the frozen A0 control at the same rung, never with the previous promotion, so small regressions accumulate against one fixed reference. Every NS-* bar of obligations.json thresholds applies as an absolute budget at P-YEAR-ONE; resource caps: memory peak within the 11 GiB reservation pool, disk peak within the 50 GiB stop line of the 60 GiB VM (lab/PLAN.md section 8).
   995	
   996	| Budget | Allowance vs A0 | Direction | Source |
   997	| --- | --- | --- | --- |
   998	| B-WRITE-BYTES-PER-FACT | 4.0 | max | provisional (RULINGS Q16): projection, indexes, journal and feed together |
   999	| B-INGEST-FACTS-PER-S | 0.5 | min | provisional (RULINGS Q16) |
  1000	| B-CURRENT-PULL-P99 | 1.0 | max | derived: the current path must not be slower than ledger-only |
  1001	| B-COMMIT-P99 | 1.25 | max | derived from NS-P1-WRITER-P99-RATIO-256 |
  1002	| B-MEMORY-PEAK | 1.5 | max | provisional (RULINGS Q16) |
  1003	| B-DISK-PEAK | 2.0 | max | provisional (RULINGS Q16) |
  1004	
