  1007	### 8.7 Composition identity (TARGETS 4.1, RULINGS Q28)
  1008	
  1009	| Item | Rule |
  1010	| --- | --- |
  1011	| assignments | source, current, history, analytics |
  1012	| engines | each assignment is XTDB or QLever |
  1013	| receiptBinding | every receipt binds, per assignment, the engine image digest, configuration hash and slot; every replication edge (feed consumer source hash, translation generation); and each serving index's watermark at read time |
  1014	| basis | a basis is a source-of-truth position (epoch, position) plus a valid time |
  1015	| watermarkRouting | a read at basis B is served by index I only if w(I) >= B.position; otherwise it waits up to T-WATERMARK-WAIT-MS and then routes to a fallback that has the position (the source of truth's own query surface or another index); the receipt records the route; no index answers for a basis it has not reached |
  1016	| ackOwnership | the source of truth sends the ACK, and only after the current index's watermark has reached the commit's position; history and analytics are asynchronous behind watermarks |
  1017	| layerSwaps | layers are swapped one at a time under matched workloads at small rungs (current-index candidates on P1 and P4; history candidates on past-basis reads and GS.12; source candidates on P2 and P3); only the two or three best compositions go on to end-to-end validation with the golden scenarios |
  1018	| scopeKey | an engine-scope receipt's key is (layer, the engine assigned to that layer, its image digest, configuration hash and slot), derived from the composition, never from engineOfLane |
