176:### 3.4 Cheapest design that meets the P3 shape
180:   BEGIN READ WRITE WITH (METADATA = {cmd, subj, pos, attrs, vf, vt})   -- entity, attributes, valid range
182:     INSERT INTO feed (_id = cmd, subj, pos, changes[ {attr, valid_from, valid_to} ])   -- same tx, atomic
187:        (resume = last processed msg_id, read inclusive and skip the duplicate; gap-free by log order)
189:   plus the content: feed row by _id = cmd (an _id lookup)   or the METADATA map itself
194:- Order and gaps: tx ids are log offsets, strictly increasing, so a checkpoint of the last `msg_id` gives exact resume. Aborted transactions must be filtered with `committed`.
195:- The `METADATA` map is the lightest carrier: one source (`xt.txs`) holds tx, entity, attributes and range with no second lookup. Its size limit and effect on `xt.txs` scan cost were not measured.
